 "answer": {
  "answer": "No timing shift or speed scaling was confirmed to make VaVAM rear-end the lead car at 2 Hz planning. None of the 5 challenging cases was confirmed, so the goal was not met. Two settings failed: 12855a41 at +2 s, 1.0x (S20) and 19f339ba at +2 s, 0.75x (S26). Even these were not rear-ends. In every failure the policy drifted left out of its lane and hit a car in the next lane, and triage puts the fault on the policy, not on rendering. S20 failed in about half of its repeats, but its range runs from well below 0.5 to well above it, so it is not confirmed. S26 rests on a single run, which is a hint, not a rate. Most other settings got only one or two runs, so the study cannot say they are safe.",
